rustfs-guide 1.0
=================
Covered RustFS version: 1.0.2 (Cargo workspace version)
Language baseline: Rust 1.99.0, edition 2024
Source snapshot: rustfs/rustfs commit 6153769 (2026-10-14)
Source material: README.md, ARCHITECTURE.md, CHANGELOG.md, docs/ (121 files),
deploy/, helm/, Docker/Compose files, and code defaults in crates/config,
crates/credentials, crates/ecstore and rustfs/src.

This guide condenses the official repository documentation and the
operator-relevant code defaults into 17 reference files. It is not a copy of
the upstream docs: normative details are summarized and linked back to the
source document or symbol.

Key boundaries at this version:
- S3 compatibility is "broad for supported features", not complete.
- ACL authorization is intentionally unsupported.
- S3 Tables (Iceberg REST) is preview.
- MinIO on-disk compatibility is read-only, one-way, feature-gated for SSE.
- FIPS 140-3 validation is not claimed.

For release changes see:
https://github.com/rustfs/rustfs/releases
